dbi-translate

This tool patches DBI but includes none of it. Users supply their own DBI NRO.

Credits and related work:

- DBI -- the Nintendo Switch homebrew installer/manager this tool patches.
  Authored by duckbill; hosted and maintained on GitHub by rashevskyv.
  https://github.com/rashevskyv/dbi

- dbi-i18n by BohdanBuinich -- the runtime-translation approach for DBI and the
  DBITRNS table format, with which this project's tables are compatible. This project
  is an independent, self-contained reimplementation (offline keystone/capstone rather
  than a devkitA64 toolchain) and shares no source with it.
  https://github.com/BohdanBuinich/dbi-i18n

- DBIPatcher by rashevskyv -- the community translation dataset and localization
  pipeline; its CSVs work directly with `build-table`.
  https://github.com/rashevskyv/DBIPatcher

- Morce3232 -- earlier DBI patching work that inspired the above.
  https://github.com/Morce3232

Vendored into DBIPatcher as vendor/dbi_translate from upstream commit
1320e138fd017db70c1436b537aef7be030f0668, with these changes:

- DBI 912 support (V912 in versions.py; the runtime lives in an unreferenced
  libde265 function because the 912 .text zero tail is too small).
- Patcher state, persistent string and scratch buffer moved past MOD0
  __bss_end__ (they overlapped the main thread's TLS string slots), MOD0
  bss_end raised to the image end so crt0 zeroes them on boot, and a build
  check that rejects any state area inside __bss_end__.
- make_pfxsfx line-length gate raised from 128 to 256 bytes.
- An exact-match hook on the std::string(const char*, size_t) copy that the
  DBI 912 game info panel uses (Version.ctors). The panel builds its labels
  (Контент, Тикеты, Язык, ...) through it, not through the `ctor` hook. DBI
  has 43 such copies; hooking all of them hangs DBI at a black screen, so
  copies are added one at a time after a console test. 912 only for now.
